<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter, Constable of Portugal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1429–1466</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter, Constable of Portugal, was a Portuguese prince and poet, son of the regent Peter, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coimbra">Coimbra</a>. In 1463 the rebel Catalans, at war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-ii-of-aragon">John II of Aragon</a>, chose him as their king; he died at Granollers in 1466 without winning the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-constable-of-portugal.jpg" alt="Peter, Constable of Portugal" width="320" height="582" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ca:user:amadalvarez · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Huguet-RetauleCondestable-7244_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
